---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "What Is a 3AM Cleaning Test? | QuietBabyGear";
const description = "QuietBabyGear's 3AM Cleaning Test explains how we measure baby gear cleanup friction under tired, low-light parent conditions.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Methodology note</p>
    <h1>What is a 3AM Cleaning Test?</h1>
    <p class="lead">A 3AM Cleaning Test is QuietBabyGear's way of measuring what happens after a baby product is used, when a parent is tired, the room is quiet, and cleanup still has to happen before the next use.</p>

    <h2>3AM is a scenario, not a literal requirement</h2>
    <p>By 3AM, we mean the low-light, half-awake parent scenario: one hand free, a quiet room, and very little patience for complicated cleanup. A product can look easy in daylight and feel very different when it has to be reset quietly at night.</p>

    <h2>What we measure</h2>
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Metric</th>
          <th>What it captures</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>MCT</td><td>How long it takes to reset the product for the next use.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>SSS</td><td>How loud or disruptive the product is in a quiet room.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>OOH</td><td>Whether the product can be started, held, or reset with one hand free.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Reset friction</td><td>Filters, chambers, warnings, drying steps, and parts that slow a tired parent down.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>What counts as cleaning reset time?</h2>
    <p>Cleaning reset time starts when use ends and stops when the product is reasonably ready to dry, store, or use again. For a manual aspirator, that may mean rinsing a few parts and replacing a disposable filter. For an electric aspirator, it may include removing the chamber, rinsing tips, avoiding backflow, and keeping the device body dry.</p>

    <h2>What this test does not claim</h2>
    <p>This test does not measure medical effectiveness, diagnose congestion, or recommend treatment. It only measures product handling and cleanup friction.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

